.TH SQRT 3M  "August 1, 1992"
.UC 6
.ds up \fIulp\fR
.SH NAME
sqrt, cbrt \- square root, cube root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.B double sqrt(double \fIx\fP);
.fi
.SH "(ALSO AVAILABLE IN BSD)"
.nf
.B double cbrt(double \fIx\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IR Sqrt ( x )
returns the square root of x.
.PP
.IR Cbrt ( x )
returns the square root of x.
.I Cbrt
is not neither ANSI- nor POSIX-compliant.
.SH ERROR (due to roundoff, etc.)
.I Sqrt
on a machine that conforms to IEEE 754 is correctly rounded
in accordance with the rounding mode in force; the error is less than
half an \*(up in the default mode (round\-to\-nearest).
An \*(up is one \fIU\fRnit in the \fIL\fRast \fIP\fRlace carried.
.PP
.I Cbrt
is accurate to within 0.7
.IR ulps .
.SH SEE ALSO
math(3M)
